; REGRESSION GATE. `display` had no 2-argument (explicit output port) form
; on the VM at all -- unlike `write`, which dispatches to _write1/_write2 by
; arity through a Scheme-level wrapper, "display" resolved straight to the
; native-211 (`print_value`, always current-output-port) preamble closure at
; EVERY arity. Calling `(display x port)` therefore invoked that arity-1
; closure with 2 arguments: an arity mismatch that silently printed `x` to
; stdout instead of `port`, left `port` untouched, AND (because the callee's
; frame only accounted for one argument) left the evaluation stack one slot
; off from that point on -- invisible when the call was a bare top-level
; statement, but corrupting whatever the result fed into once used in
; expression position (an argument to another call, a `let` binding
; consumed later, even a bare variable reference read back afterward).
; Found while adding R7RS 7.1.1 |...| symbol tests that exercised this exact
; shape. Fixed by giving `display` a real 2-argument compiler special case
; (mirroring the existing 1-argument one) that emits native 2226
; (_display2), the `display`-flavoured (write_syntax=0) twin of _write2/618
; -- same underlying vm_write_value_port(), just without write's quotes/bars.

(define (capture x)
  (let ((port (open-output-string)))
    (display x port)
    (get-output-string port)))

; Bare statement position (this shape always worked -- kept as a control).
(let ((port (open-output-string)))
  (display "hello" port)
  (display (get-output-string port)))
(newline)

; Expression position: the captured string flows into further computation.
; This is exactly the shape that silently produced "" (port never written)
; before the fix.
(display (capture "hello"))
(newline)
(display (capture 42))
(newline)
(display (capture (quote foo)))
(newline)
(display (capture (list 1 2 3)))
(newline)

; The stack-imbalance half: a SECOND, unrelated computation performed right
; after the corrupting call must see correct values, not whatever the stray
; slot left behind.
(display (+ 1 (string-length (capture "ab"))))
(newline)

; Passed straight into another call's argument list (not just a `let`).
(display (string-append "[" (capture "x") "]"))
(newline)

; display to a port must not add write's quoting/escaping -- the one
; difference from _write2/618.
(display (capture "has \"quotes\" and \\backslash\\"))
(newline)
